{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Fridge UI guard",
  "description": "When the UI changes: check escaping, layering, the storage schema, the light colourful theme and accessibility.",
  "version": "1",
  "when": {
    "type": "fileEdited",
    "patterns": ["app.js", "index.html", "style.css"]
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "A UI file (app.js, index.html or style.css) was just edited. Review only the changed parts against .kiro/steering/fridge-graveyard.md:\n- Security: every user-provided string inserted via innerHTML goes through esc(). No network calls, no remote scripts or images.\n- Layering: business rules (dates, status, matching, stats) live in logic.js, not app.js. Every state change calls saveState() and then render().\n- Storage: if the state shape changed, SCHEMA_VERSION is bumped and Fridge.sanitiseState still reads old backups.\n- Theme: white background, colour tokens only (--green/--orange/--purple/--red/--blue and their -tint), consistent colour meaning, ink-on-tint contrast >= 4.5:1, a dark overlay for text on photos. New images are local files in assets/ with alt=\"\" (or real alt text if they carry meaning) and loading=\"lazy\" below the fold.\n- Accessibility: labelled inputs, aria-label with the item name on icon buttons, status not conveyed by colour or emoji alone, emoji aria-hidden, a visible focus ring, 44 px targets, no horizontal scroll at 360 px.\nFix clear violations directly. Reply with a short list: OK items, and anything you fixed or that needs a decision."
  }
}
